{{- /* Rendered into both ~/.config/fd/ignore and ~/.config/git/ignore.
       The fd copy is also pulled into rg via --ignore-file in ripgreprc, so
       these rules apply to fd, rg and git alike, from any directory — unlike
       ~/.ignore, which only bites when the search starts at $HOME.

       Scope: generated artifacts and VCS metadata, i.e. things unwanted both
       when committing and when searching. Bulky home directories that are
       merely uninteresting go in dot_ignore.tmpl instead, so that searching
       from inside them still works. */ -}}
